  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e02c375b071ccc34381cd4e8e70fd2af, type: 3}
  m_Name: Readme
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: com.fuzzphyte.utility.editor::FuzzPhyte.Utility.Editor.FPReadmeAsset
  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: b521bf5d6ffa177458e7c14188bbf89d, type: 3}
  title: FuzzPhyte Model Viewer
  subtitle: A high level package that brings placement, orbital camera tools, updated
    input system, UI Toolkit, and other FuzzPhyte utility libraries together to showcase
    a catalog based model viewer.
  version: 0.0.1
  overview: 'FP Model Viewer is a data-driven Unity package for turning scene objects
    and prefabs into deployable model catalogs. Its Editor builder uses FP Placement
    display data to calculate model bounds, frame a capture camera, generate selected
    face and corner thumbnails, create viewer-item and catalog ScriptableObjects,
    preserve optional FP Tag metadata, and prepare imported meshes for runtime access.

    At
    runtime, FP Model Viewer builds a configurable, paged UI Toolkit catalog with
    responsive styling, joined tag filtering, item-detail thumbnails, prefab spawning,
    catalog visibility controls, interaction events, and optional OBJ downloads.

    The
    package composes FP Placement for model metadata and orbital-camera behavior,
    FP UI for its UI Toolkit foundation, and FP Utility for shared data, tags, mesh
    packaging, and platform-specific file delivery.'
  overviewLinks:
  - label: Documentation
    url: https://github.com/JShull/FP_ModelViewer/blob/main/README.md
  - label: Model View Sample
    url: https://github.com/JShull/FP_ModelViewer/tree/main/Samples~/ModelViewerEx
  - label: Open Model Viewer Builder
    url: menu:FuzzPhyte/Model Viewer/Builder
  sections:
  - heading: Build a Model Catalog
    showSeparatorBefore: 0
    body: 'Open the Model Viewer Builder and choose an output folder and FP_ModelCaptureProfile,
      then add scene objects or prefab assets as sources. Every source requires an
      FP_ModelDisplayBinding with an assigned FP_ModelDisplayData asset. Auto Setup
      Missing can calculate renderer bounds, create the required display-data asset,
      and assign the binding automatically.

      Choose any combination of the
      14 supported face and corner thumbnail views, select a cover view, and optionally
      assign up to three reusable FP Tag assets to each source. The builder generates
      one FP_ModelViewerItemData asset per source and combines those items into an
      ordered FP_ModelViewerCatalogData asset.

      Each viewer item stores its
      display data, included prefab, tags, thumbnails, cover and default views, and
      optional external asset information. Scene-only objects are saved as reusable
      viewer prefabs. Imported model meshes are also prepared for runtime Read/Write
      access when possible.'
    links:
    - label: Catalog Documentation
      url: https://github.com/JShull/FP_ModelViewer/blob/main/README.md#building-a-catalog
  - heading: Configure the Runtime UI
    showSeparatorBefore: 1
    body: 'Add a UIDocument and FP_ModelViewerGridUI to a scene object, assign the
      document and generated catalog, and then choose the number of rows and columns
      to display per panel. The viewer calculates the required number of panels automatically
      and generates only cells that contain real catalog items.

      Container
      Insets position the complete viewer within a percentage of the available screen.
      Branding settings control the catalog title and an optional top-left, top-center,
      or top-right logo. Item Cell, Button, Popup, and Tag Filter settings control
      colors, rounded corners, outlines, hover and selected states, popup presentation,
      filter columns, text truncation, and scrolling.

      The catalog supports
      joined tag filtering, so an item must contain every selected tag to remain
      visible. It can also hide after spawning an item and provide a compact control
      for restoring the catalog. Assign Spawn Target to define where selected included
      prefabs are placed.

      A custom stylesheet is optional. The generated interface
      includes a complete inline layout and stable USS class names for projects that
      require additional styling.'
    links:
    - label: Runtime UI Documentation
      url: https://github.com/JShull/FP_ModelViewer/blob/main/README.md#runtime-ui-settings
  - heading: Respon to Item Selection and Actions
    showSeparatorBefore: 1
    body: 'Clicking a catalog cell selects its FP_ModelViewerItemData and invokes
      On Item Selected. When Show Popup On Selection is enabled, the same interaction
      opens a detail popup containing every thumbnail stored for that item. SelectedItem
      remains available to code so camera controllers, information panels, analytics,
      audio, or other systems can respond to the active model.

      The built-in
      popup provides Back to Catalog, Spawn Item, and optional Download OBJ actions.
      Inspector events are available for item selection, popup closure, item spawning
      and removal, page changes, grid rebuilding, tag-filter changes, catalog visibility,
      dedicated catalog-hidden and catalog-visible screen regions, and OBJ export
      success or failure.

      Matching C# events are available when another runtime
      system owns the behavior. FP Model Viewer publishes the selected data and interaction
      lifecycle while the application decides how its camera, panels, downloads,
      or other features should respond.'
    links:
    - label: Section & Events
      url: https://github.com/JShull/FP_ModelViewer/blob/main/README.md#item-selection-actions-and-events
